[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Epoch API Admission and Adaptive Diagnostics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-API-002
TITLE: Inclusive request identity and joint charge refusal
STATEMENT: >>>
The API shall accept and preserve a 256-byte nonempty case identifier and reject
257 bytes. A charged junction shall not prohibit a DC operating point, and an
explicit initial state shall remain supported for a linear RC transient. The
existing charged-junction plus explicit-state dynamic refusal shall remain a
joint predicate rather than refusing either independently valid use case.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-TRACE-002
TITLE: Truthful adaptive rejection diagnostics
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: >>>
Inferred diagnostic contract: the structured DEBUG event
adaptive_local_error_rejected shall be emitted only when the scaled local
error exceeds one. It shall report the actual scaled_error. An exactly-one
accepted boundary shall not be described as rejected. This finite-scenario
verification does not establish a public stable log schema or a unique
tie-breaking rule for equally worst unknowns.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/epoch_api_admission.rs and
src/adaptive.rs rejection_event_records_only_errors_strictly_above_one.
Counterparts are replayed against the later development tests without changing
the frozen 4,411-candidate source or its historical results. A reviewed equal-
norm tie choice may change diagnostic row identity while preserving the norm.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-ERROR-002
TITLE: Finite operands do not authorize nonfinite error calculations
STATEMENT: >>>
Adaptive error estimation shall fail with InvalidInput when a computed tolerance
scale or discrepancy is nonfinite, even if both trial operands and supplied
tolerances are finite. An overflowed denominator shall not turn an unknown
error into a successful zero; an overflowed difference shall not return a
successful infinite norm.
<<<
